# Build outputs, not source. `scripts/export_model.py` regenerates everything
# here from a config (plus a checkpoint, once one exists).
#
# Worth being explicit about why these must never be committed: the .onnx files
# currently in here hold RANDOMLY INITIALISED weights, because no model has been
# trained. A committed random-weight engine is exactly the kind of artifact that
# later gets mistaken for a trained one.
*.onnx
*.engine
*.plan
*.trt
